00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Canada's 40% export surge to China this year gives TFSA holders a fresh window to tilt toward commodity-exposed holdings. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 233. Bank of America's consolidated Edison call, the Post-Earnings target-raised process, and a quarterly review on a registered account, plus market pulse and the practice investment. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.620
no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor and this isn't financial advice. Always

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:41.111
do your own research before putting real money to work. Shipments of Canadian resources and

00:00:41.111 --> 00:00:46.931
manufactured goods, BNN Bloomberg reports outpace growth to any other major market across

00:00:46.931 --> 00:00:51.891
the first nine months of the year. That window is the measuring stick for whether the trend holds

00:00:51.891 --> 00:00:56.551
into the final quarter, and it is the moment to check whether names with meaningful China

00:00:56.551 --> 00:00:59.571
revenue still sit inside the weights you already wrote down.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:10.393
The Standard &amp; Poor's 500, or S&amp;P 500, closed at 7,562, down 0.4%, while the NASDAQ composite

00:01:10.393 --> 00:01:21.173
closed at 25,136, down 0.9%, up 8.18% year-to-date, and up 12.34% since the practice book opened

00:01:21.173 --> 00:01:23.073
on March 16, 2026.

00:01:23.073 --> 00:01:32.553
The Toronto Stock Exchange Composite, or TSX Composite, closed at 36,106 down 0.1% with

00:01:32.553 --> 00:01:38.073
TSX futures slipping on softer oil and gold as US futures pointed lower ahead of NVIDIA

00:01:38.073 --> 00:01:40.693
earnings and anthropics expected debut.

00:01:41.253 --> 00:01:46.853
Statistics Canada releases October inflation figures today, with energy prices still elevated,

00:01:47.413 --> 00:01:51.853
so Bank of Canada and Federal Reserve paths stay in focus for rate-sensitive names.

00:01:51.853 --> 00:01:57.513
14 days ago, the simulated book bought H on Utilities Infrastructure as rate visibility

00:01:57.513 --> 00:02:01.633
improved, and that hold finished up 4.74%.

00:02:01.633 --> 00:02:07.226
Bank of America lifted its consolidated Edison target after the earnings beat, and that

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:12.526
is the valuation reset signal the post-earnings price target upgrade process is built to catch.

00:02:13.026 --> 00:02:18.586
Screen for a new target that implies at least 10% upside from the prior close, then confirmed

00:02:18.586 --> 00:02:23.586
the revision followed actual reported results rather than forward guidance alone, because

00:02:23.586 --> 00:02:27.546
a number written after the books are closed is a different animal than a number written

00:02:27.546 --> 00:02:32.546
on a slide deck. Think of it like a home appraisal after the renovation is actually finished.

00:02:33.026 --> 00:02:37.666
The appraiser only raises the figure once they have walked the rooms, not when the contractor

00:02:37.666 --> 00:02:42.666
emails a promise, and a post earnings target raise is that walk through while a guidance

00:02:42.666 --> 00:02:48.586
only revision is the email. Enter only when the shares sit within 3% of the 50-day average,

00:02:49.066 --> 00:02:54.346
so the reset is not already fully in the price, and write down the pre-revision consensus in

00:02:54.346 --> 00:02:58.646
the same sitting so you can measure the upgrade against the share price reaction over the next

00:02:58.646 --> 00:03:04.426
sessions. You see a utility print a target raise and the stock already sits well above that 50-day

00:03:04.426 --> 00:03:11.146
band. Do you chase it or stand down? Stand down. The proximity filter exists so you are not paying for

00:03:11.146 --> 00:03:16.186
a re-rating that already happened. The same process worked in earlier utility resets when

00:03:16.186 --> 00:03:20.926
rate visibility improved, and it failed when the revision rested only on cost-cutting

00:03:20.926 --> 00:03:26.186
assumptions with no volume behind it. Pull the exact target change on the investing.com

00:03:26.186 --> 00:03:31.806
analyst ratings page, or your broker's research feed, compare it to that pre-earnings consensus

00:03:31.806 --> 00:03:37.166
in one step, and treat higher than average volume on the earnings day as the tell that institutional

00:03:37.166 --> 00:03:41.706
desks are rebalancing after the print. Canadian investors can run the whole

00:03:41.706 --> 00:03:47.466
sequence inside a tax-free savings account, or TFSA, without an immediate tax hit,

00:03:47.846 --> 00:03:52.366
so any re-rating compounds in the account rather than on a T-slip. Write the

00:03:52.366 --> 00:03:56.426
consensus down before the revision, or you cannot tell whether the upgrade did

00:03:56.426 --> 00:04:02.854
any work. The simulated weekly hold is consolidated Edison, ticker ED, listed on

00:04:02.854 --> 00:04:08.574
The New York Stock Exchange, or NYSE, in utilities, and it is a learning trade with no real

00:04:08.574 --> 00:04:09.414
money attached.

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:15.114
It demonstrates the post-earnings price target upgrade process in one clause, then adds

00:04:15.114 --> 00:04:17.154
the pieces that process does not set.

00:04:17.594 --> 00:04:23.854
A 6% stop below entry that caps the simulated loss at $60 USD on the $1,000 position.

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:31.834
A target of plus 2% to plus 5% over 5 sessions, if follow through buying shows up, and an invalidation

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:36.194
that fires if the shares close under the lowest print of the three sessions that ran just

00:04:36.194 --> 00:04:37.874
before the upgrade hit the tape.

00:04:38.474 --> 00:04:41.374
Entry is the next session's open under the published rules.

00:04:41.874 --> 00:04:46.634
The hold runs five sessions or hits the stop, whichever comes first, and it is scored

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:51.574
against the NASDAQ composite over those same sessions, with no discretionary exit.

00:04:52.134 --> 00:04:57.374
Confidence is medium, the earnings beat and the target raise are confirmed, yet rate-sensitive

00:04:57.374 --> 00:05:03.214
of utilities still face broader rotation pressure, and a medium grade is exactly two aligned factors

00:05:03.214 --> 00:05:08.574
without one uncertainty left hanging. The technical side is a stock near its 50-day average

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:14.454
with no extreme relative strength index or RSI reading, and volume on the reaction day above

00:05:14.454 --> 00:05:19.454
the recent average, which is the volume filter the older cost-cutting failures did not have.

00:05:20.054 --> 00:05:25.574
Valuation discipline is the lesson tag on this one. The 50-day proximity filter keeps momentum

00:05:25.574 --> 00:05:30.314
them only names out. The invalidation is written before the simulated money is at risk,

00:05:30.674 --> 00:05:35.074
and the five-session clock removes the urge to rewrite the thesis when the tape gets noisy.

00:05:35.814 --> 00:05:41.014
Prior utility resets paid when rate visibility improved, and they did not pay when the note

00:05:41.014 --> 00:05:46.054
was only a cost cut story, so this hold is allowed to run because the beat and the volume

00:05:46.054 --> 00:05:50.854
filter are present, and it will be graded against those same tests when the five sessions are

00:05:50.854 --> 00:05:55.177
done. Yahoo Finance Canada quote pages put real-time quotes,

00:05:55.177 --> 00:06:00.057
historical charts, and analyst target changes for a listed security in one view,

00:06:00.457 --> 00:06:04.277
and the free tier covers the major exchanges including TSX names.

00:06:04.857 --> 00:06:09.477
Canadian investors can set price alerts and export the data table straight into a spreadsheet

00:06:09.477 --> 00:06:15.157
for a quarterly review without retyping prices or dates, and the same page overlays volume

00:06:15.157 --> 00:06:19.477
trends and moving averages so you can check whether a target revision is happening near a

00:06:19.477 --> 00:06:20.737
technically relevant level.

00:06:21.873 --> 00:06:26.933
Investing.com's analyst ratings feed surfaces price target changes and earnings beat notes

00:06:26.933 --> 00:06:27.713
within minutes.

00:06:28.113 --> 00:06:31.133
Let's you filter by sector and sort by implied upside.

00:06:31.613 --> 00:06:36.333
And shows how many analysts sit in each consensus so you can see whether one house is dragging

00:06:36.333 --> 00:06:38.833
the number or the desk is moving together.

00:06:39.393 --> 00:06:43.893
Sorting that list by sector and then by upside produces a short list you can cross-check

00:06:43.893 --> 00:06:46.493
against the 50-day average rule in under two minutes.

00:06:46.493 --> 00:06:51.673
and I have no financial relationship with Yahoo Finance Canada or Investing.com.

